{"meta":{"lessonId":"grade_5_math_ch11_seg12","grade":5,"subject":"math","language":"en","topic":"Connect & Create: Geometric Collage","chapterTitle":"Ch.11 · Geometric Galaxy: Shapes and Spaces","minutes":40,"sloDescriptions":["I can find the area of a triangle with half base times height, and of a parallelogram with base times height."],"source":"v9_html","adapterV":2},"goal":"I can find the area of a triangle with half base times height, and of a parallelogram with base times height.","sloFull":"I can find the area of a triangle with half base times height, and of a parallelogram with base times height.","sloCode":"M-05-GE-02","hook":{"minutes":4,"warmUp":{"teacherAsks":"Say together: the area formula of a triangle, and of a parallelogram.","expectedAnswer":"Triangle: half times base times height. Parallelogram: base times height."},"conversation":[{"teacherAsks":"Open textbook p.252. Look at the house and the sailboat. Which shapes do you see — triangles, rectangles, parallelograms? Show me with your fingers (3 fingers = triangle, 4 = rectangle)."}],"steps":[{"n":1,"action":"Open book to p.252. Point to the roof and the sail in the picture."},{"n":2,"action":"Ask: is a triangle's area the same as a rectangle's, or half? Thumbs up for half, thumbs down for same."}],"keyWords":[{"term":"triangle","def":"Area = 1/2 x base x height."},{"term":"parallelogram","def":"Area = base x height."},{"term":"collage","def":"A picture made from pieces of recycled paper and card."}],"materials":["textbook p.252","chalk","board","copies"]},"iDo":{"minutes":8,"steps":[{"n":1,"action":"On the board draw a rectangle 8 cm by 5 cm, then a line corner to corner showing the triangle is half of it."},{"n":2,"say":"Page 252 shows a house with a triangular roof but no numbers, so we pick base 8 cm, height 5 cm. Rectangle area = 8 x 5 = 40 cm2."},{"n":3,"say":"Triangle = 1/2 x 8 x 5 = 20 cm2. A parallelogram has no half: base x height only."},{"n":4,"say":"Check yourself: is my shape a triangle? Then I halve. Is it a parallelogram? No halving."}],"cfu":"CFU: Triangle base 6 cm, height 4 cm. Why do we halve for a triangle but not a parallelogram? Expected: a triangle is half its rectangle. Area = 1/2 x 6 x 4 = 12 cm2.","misconception":{"slip":"Writing base x height for a triangle with no half.","fix":"Ask: does it fill the whole rectangle or half? Triangle halves, parallelogram does not."}},"weDo":{"minutes":12,"strategy":"Group by level, by row. Each row gets its own task written in their copy, checked by choral answer and show-of-copy.","steps":[{"n":1,"action":"Row 1 (needs support): in the copy, draw the rectangle for a triangle with base 8 cm, height 4 cm. Find rectangle area (8x4) together, then halve together."},{"n":2,"action":"Row 2 (on level): sailboat sail on p.252, base 10 cm height 6 cm — write A = 1/2 x 10 x 6 in the copy, solve together."},{"n":3,"action":"Row 3 (ahead): window pane as parallelogram, base 7 cm height 3 cm — write A = 7 x 3 in the copy, then also find a triangle with the same base and height and compare the two areas."},{"n":4,"say":"Whole class CFU together: triangle base 12 cm height 5 cm — what is the area, and is it 60? Show thumbs down for 60, up for 30."}]},"youDo":{"minutes":12,"steps":[{"n":1,"action":"Every child works alone in the copy."},{"n":2,"action":"If stuck, child checks: is it a triangle? Then halve."}],"problems":[{"n":1,"prompt":"Zainab makes a triangular flag for her collage border: base 10 cm, height 4 cm. Find its area.","answer":"1/2 x 10 x 4 = 20 cm2."},{"n":2,"prompt":"Usman cuts a parallelogram piece: base 9 cm, height 5 cm. Find its area.","answer":"9 x 5 = 45 cm2."},{"n":3,"prompt":"Triangle base 12 cm, height 8 cm. Find its area.","answer":"1/2 x 12 x 8 = 48 cm2."},{"n":4,"prompt":"Stretch: Look at the roof gable picture on p.252. If base is 6 cm and height 3 cm, find the triangle's area, then find the area of a parallelogram with the same base and height. Explain why the two answers differ.","answer":"Triangle: 1/2 x 6 x 3 = 9 cm2. Parallelogram: 6 x 3 = 18 cm2. Triangle is half because it only fills half its rectangle."}]},"wrap":{"minutes":4,"exitOptions":[{"prompt":"Thumbs up, sideways or down: 'I can pick the right formula and give area with its unit.' Then solve: (1) Triangle base 12 cm, height 8 cm. (2) Parallelogram base 6 cm, height 4 cm.","answer":"(1) 48 cm2. (2) 24 cm2."}],"reteach":"Triangle: area = 1/2 x base x height. Parallelogram: area = base x height, no half.","homework":["Find one object at home shaped like a triangle or parallelogram (roof, window, folded box). Measure base and height in cm and find its area.","Draw and label one triangle and one parallelogram with their areas, for your collage page."]}}
